From 38acc638c1b5c2ba7937135fedc1be141993ffcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chaton <definitelyfrenchname@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 12:44:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cps2w: the WIDE v1 machine entry and the MANDATORY QSound
 trim in the MRA

The Vampire Saved WIDE v1 romset cannot be downloaded to MiSTer as a
straight concatenation on ANY SDRAM tier: mapped verbatim the image is
70.26 MB, which overflows BOTH the 26-bit game-side port
(`modules/jtframe/hdl/inc/jtframe_mem_ports.inc:1`, `input [25:0]
ioctl_addr` = 64 MB) and the 16-bit region-start word the header carries
(`set_header_offset`, corerom.go). The MRA has to trim, and this commit is
that trim -- no RTL, no romset change.

WHAT IS ADDED

* `doc/mame.xml` gains a `vsavjw` machine entry: `vsavj`'s, verbatim except
  for the ROM map, the description and `sourcefile="capcom/cps2w.cpp"`.
  That sourcefile tag is the gate: `cores/cps2` parses
  `sourcefile=["cps2.cpp"]`, which does not match it, so the reference core
  cannot see the WIDE set and keeps emitting exactly its 316 MRAs. Measured:
  `jtframe mra cps2` -> 316 MRAs, none of them WIDE; `jtframe mra cps2w` ->
  8, and the stock `vsavj` MRA is still byte-identical to `cps2`'s except
  `<rbf>`.

* `cores/cps2w/cfg/mame2mra.toml` opts in with
  `sourcefile=[ "cps2.cpp", "cps2w.cpp" ]` and gains a `qsoundw` region:
  skipped for every set (`{ name="qsoundw", skip=true }`, so no stock MRA
  moves by a byte) and, for `setname="vsavjw"`, a `parts=` byte window into
  `vsw.21m` of `length=0x0F0000` -- DSP sample banks 0x80-0x8E, the first
  sample-bank boundary above the last live byte (`0x8E57F0`). `vsw.22m` is
  not mapped at all. The romset keeps both members, for FBNeo and MAME.

WHY A SEPARATE REGION RATHER THAN `parts=` ON `qsound`

`parse_parts` puts EVERY part inside ONE `<interleave>` when `width>8`
(corerom.go), and `interleave2rom` then resolves each output lane to the
FIRST finger that claims it -- so three members that all carry `map="12"`
would collapse to the first one, truncated to the shortest. Splitting the
extension into its own region keeps the stock 8 MB on the generic path,
where it is emitted exactly as `cores/cps2` emits it, and leaves the
trimmed member alone in a region where a single-part `parts=` is correct.

`rom_len` is NOT usable to shorten: it advances `pos` by the full file size
regardless, which would desynchronise every later header word from the real
`.rom`.

MEASURED, against jotego/jtcores v1.7.3 + this branch

  rom/vsavjw.rom = 66,265,152 B (63.196 MB), 843,712 B under the 64 MB
  ioctl_addr ceiling; header words audiocpu 6144 / qsound 6400 / gfx 15552 /
  firmware 64704 KiB, all < 65,536; every region start 1 KiB-aligned in
  bulk_addr terms. Every region was verified byte-for-byte against the zips,
  and the trimmed QSound region is a PURE TRUNCATION of the untrimmed one.

NOTE FOR ANYONE READING THIS OUT OF CONTEXT: jtframe locates zip members by
CRC32 and by nothing else (mra2rom.go:163-172). FBNeo and MAME resolve by
NAME and only warn on a hash mismatch, which is why the WIDE members carry
sentinel CRCs in both of those drivers. Here the CRCs must be the real ones
of the built romset, so the entry above is GENERATED from the zip by
tools/gen_vsavjw_xml.py in the Vampire Saved repository, and a gate there
fails if a rebuild moves one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C93kTvSDUfHLL5sbjrArzn
---
 cores/cps2w/cfg/mame2mra.toml | 55 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 doc/mame.xml                  | 67 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 120 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cores/cps2w/cfg/mame2mra.toml b/cores/cps2w/cfg/mame2mra.toml
index 4b3e09525..9d1b3066d 100644
--- a/cores/cps2w/cfg/mame2mra.toml
+++ b/cores/cps2w/cfg/mame2mra.toml
@@ -3,7 +3,13 @@ mraauthor=["jotego,atrac17"]
 zip.alt="qsound.zip"
 
 [parse]
-sourcefile=[ "cps2.cpp" ]
+# "cps2w.cpp" is not a MAME source file: it is the tag the project's own
+# `vsavjw` entry carries in jtframe's machine catalogue (doc/mame.xml,
+# generated by tools/gen_vsavjw_xml.py in the Vampire Saved repo). The
+# reference core parses sourcefile=["cps2.cpp"], which does not match it, so
+# the WIDE set is invisible to cores/cps2 BY CONSTRUCTION and that core stays
+# untouched — the same profile-gating discipline the FBNeo and MAME legs use.
+sourcefile=[ "cps2.cpp", "cps2w.cpp" ]
 # jtcps2w: only the Vampire Savior family (vsav + clones, incl. vsavj) —
 # the stock reference leg of this core. The Vampire Saved set is added later.
 mustbe.machines=[ "vsav" ]
@@ -106,6 +112,51 @@ regions=[
     # { name="qsound",   width=16, reverse=true, machine="nwarr" },
     # { name="qsound",   width=16, reverse=true, machine="progear" },
 
+    # ── CPS-2 WIDE v1: the MiSTer QSound TRIM (14z-107 slice D0) ──────────
+    # docs/project/mister_map.md §2/§3/§7 in the Vampire Saved repo.
+    #
+    # `qsoundw` is NOT a MAME region. MAME's vsavjw puts all four QSound
+    # members in `qsound`; the project's machine entry splits the EXTENSION
+    # member out so the MRA can place a byte WINDOW into it while the stock
+    # 8 MB above it stays mapped exactly as cores/cps2 maps it. Every other
+    # set skips the region (the row below), so no stock MRA changes by a byte.
+    #
+    # THE TRIM IS MANDATORY, NOT AN OPTIMISATION. Mapped verbatim the WIDE
+    # image is 70.26 MB, which overflows BOTH the 26-bit game-side port
+    # (modules/jtframe/hdl/inc/jtframe_mem_ports.inc:1 `input [25:0]
+    # ioctl_addr` = 64 MB) and the 16-bit region-start word in the header
+    # (set_header_offset, corerom.go). Trimmed to the top of DSP sample bank
+    # 0x8E the image is 63.196 MB and all four header words are legal.
+    # `vsw.22m` is not declared at all and the tail of `vsw.21m` is not
+    # mapped; the ROMSET keeps both members, for FBNeo and MAME.
+    #
+    # `rom_len` MUST NOT be used to shorten a region: corerom.go advances
+    # `pos` by the full file size regardless, so every later header word would
+    # desynchronise from the real .rom. `parts=` is the shortening mechanism
+    # (mra2rom.go:177-196 implements the byte window).
+    #
+    # The map string is spelled out because parse_parts does NOT apply
+    # `reverse` — "12" is what the generic 16-bit path emits under
+    # reverse=true, i.e. what cores/cps2 already produces for vm3.11m/12m.
+    #
+    # length 0x0F0000: DSP sample banks 0x80-0x8E inclusive. Live content ends
+    # at region offset 0x8E57F0, inside bank 0x8E, so this covers every live
+    # byte, ends on a sample-bank boundary and keeps every later region start
+    # 1 KiB-aligned — which is what makes the header words correct at all (the
+    # Go generator's `pos` counts the 20-byte key, the RTL's `bulk_addr` does
+    # not; they agree only through that alignment).
+    #
+    # THE CRC IS THE BUILD'S, AND IT HAS TO BE. jtframe resolves zip members
+    # by CRC32 alone (mra2rom.go:163-172) — unlike FBNeo and MAME, which
+    # resolve by NAME and only warn, which is why the WIDE members carry
+    # sentinel hashes in both drivers. A romset rebuild that moves this CRC
+    # must move this row; tests/test_mister_mra_map.sh fails loudly if it does
+    # not, and tools/gen_vsavjw_xml.py regenerates the catalogue entry.
+    { name="qsoundw", skip=true },
+    { name="qsoundw", width=16, setname="vsavjw", parts=[
+        { name="vsw.21m", crc="f6c937e1", map="12", length=0x0F0000, offset=0 },
+    ] },
+
     { name="gfx",      width=64 },
     { name="firmware", files=[ { name="dl-1425.bin", crc="d6cf5ef5", size=0x2000 } ], rom_len=0x2000 },
     { name="aboardplds", skip=true },
@@ -117,7 +168,7 @@ regions=[
 order=[
     "key",
     "maincpu",
-    "audiocpu", "qsound",
+    "audiocpu", "qsound", "qsoundw",
     "gfx",
     "firmware"
 ]
